@startuml ICNNA_snirf_classes
' ============================================================
' ICNNA — +icnna.data.snirf class diagram
' Scope: +icnna/+data/+snirf (SNIRF file format adapter)
' Companion to the core spine class diagram
' Phase 3b deliverable — Item F
' ============================================================
' Log:
'   2026-06-16: FOE/Claude — File created. Current snapshot of
'       all 8 snirf classes + v2.0.0 projection notes for
'       relationsManager-mediated bridge to core.
' ============================================================
' Source: src/+icnna/+data/+snirf/@*/*.m (v1.4.1-beta)
' ============================================================
' Conventions:
'   - These classes do NOT inherit from identifiableObject.
'   - They follow the SNIRF specification directly.
'   - All are value classes (no handles).
'   - Only key properties shown; optional properties omitted
'     for clarity (see source files for full list).
' ============================================================

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 30

title ICNNA — +icnna.data.snirf classes\n8 classes (all existing at v1.4.1-beta)\nSNIRF file format adapter layer

package "+icnna.data.snirf" as snirfpkg {

  class snirf {
    +formatVersion : char
    +nirs : nirsDataset[]
    --
    +nNirsDatasets : int {Dependent}
    ==
    +load(filename) : snirf {Static}
    +save(filename)
    +readHD5file(filename) {Static}
  }

  class nirsDataset {
    +metaDataTags : metaDataTags
    +data : dataBlock[]
    +stim : stim[]
    +probe : probe
    +aux : auxBlock[]
  }

  class dataBlock {
    +dataTimeSeries : double[M x N]
    +time : double[M x 1]
    +measurementList : measurement[]
  }

  class measurement {
    +sourceIndex : int
    +detectorIndex : int
    +wavelengthIndex : int
    +dataType : int
    +dataTypeIndex : int
    ..optional (flagVisible)..
    +wavelengthActual : double
    +dataUnit : char
    +dataTypeLabel : char
    +sourcePower : double
    +detectorGain : double
    +moduleIndex : int
  }

  class probe {
    +wavelengths : double[]
    +sourcePos2D : double[S x 2]
    +sourcePos3D : double[S x 3]
    +detectorPos2D : double[D x 2]
    +detectorPos3D : double[D x 3]
    ..optional (flagVisible)..
    +wavelengthsEmission : double[]
    +sourceLabels : string[]
    +detectorLabels : string[]
    +landmarkPos2D/3D : double[]
    +landmarkLabels : string[]
    +useLocalIndex : double
  }

  class stim {
    +name : char
    +data : double[M x 3]
    ..optional (flagVisible)..
    +dataLabels : string[]
  }

  class auxBlock {
    +name : char
    +dataTimeSeries : double[M x N]
    +time : double[M x 1]
    ..optional (flagVisible)..
    +dataUnit : char
    +timeOffset : double[]
  }

  class metaDataTags {
    +subjectID : char
    +measurementDate : datetime
    +measurementTime : datetime
    +lengthUnit : char
    +timeUnit : char
    +frequencyUnit : char
    -additional : struct
    ==
    +setField(name, value)
    +getField(name) : any
    +removeField(name)
    +hasField(name) : bool
  }

}

' ================================================================
' COMPOSITION (SNIRF hierarchy)
' ================================================================
snirf         *-- "0..*" nirsDataset : nirs
nirsDataset   *-- "1"    metaDataTags : metaDataTags
nirsDataset   *-- "0..*" dataBlock : data
nirsDataset   *-- "0..*" stim : stim
nirsDataset   *-- "1"    probe : probe
nirsDataset   *-- "0..*" auxBlock : aux
dataBlock     *-- "0..*" measurement : measurementList

' ================================================================
' NOTES
' ================================================================

note top of snirfpkg
  **SNIRF file format adapter layer.**
  These 8 classes mirror the Shared Near
  Infrared Spectroscopy Format (SNIRF)
  specification 1:1.
  ..
  **NOT part of the core domain model.**
  None inherit from identifiableObject.
  They are independent value classes that
  faithfully represent .snirf file content.
  ..
  **Bridge to +data/+core:**
  Conversion functions in +op/+snirf/
  translate between snirf objects and
  ICNNA's domain entities (structuredData,
  timeline, condition, nirsMontage, etc.).
  ..
  **Optional property pattern:**
  measurement, probe, stim, auxBlock use
  a flagVisible struct to track which
  optional SNIRF fields are present.
  Methods: isproperty(), rmproperty().
end note

note as v200note #FFFFCC
  **v2.0.0 projection — relationsManager impact:**
  ..
  The snirf classes themselves remain largely
  unchanged (they mirror an external spec).
  ..
  The conversion bridge (+op/+snirf/) simplifies:
  - snirf2nirsNeuroimage creates core entities
    and registers relations via relationsManager
    instead of manually wiring *IDs.
  - Timeline/condition/montage bindings become
    relationsManager.add() calls.
  - Device linkage via manager (device relation
    registered, not stored as IDs on entities).
  ..
  **Legacy adapter (@rawData_Snirf in oo/):**
  Retained during transition. At v1.8.0
  (legacy removal), its import/export/convert
  logic migrates to +op/+snirf/ or +io/.
end note

note bottom of metaDataTags
  Dynamic field system: additional
  user-defined metadata stored as
  struct fields. subsref/subsasgn
  overloaded for dot-syntax access.
  Replaces earlier dictionary-based
  implementation (v1.1).
end note

@enduml
